Why do you want the wrapper implementing `DerefMut`?

Won't this allow `Acquired` to be updated to something that doesn't match what the dev locks?

  ```rust
  let mut quote = tx.get_mint_quote(&a).await?.ok_or(Error::UnknownQuote)?;
  quote.id = b;
  quote.add_payment(...)?;
  tx.update_mint_quote(&mut quote).await?; // writes b, we only locked a
  ```

> @thesimplekid thanks, good catch. Narrowed it in [97d3ed4](https://github.com/cashubtc/cdk/commit/97d3ed47ed1ea161709902a6933f09c416e9316f): a stored `Pending` proof with no `used_by_operation` is now moved to `Unspent` when the mint reports it unspent. Only the state is updated (`update_proofs_state`), so its derivation index and other metadata stay as they are. `Reserved`, `PendingSpent` and operation-owned `Pending` proofs are still left to their operations, and the scan totals are unchanged

